  "steps": [
    {
      "t": "Sauté aromatics",
      "x": "Sauté mode, highest setting. Heat oil, add onion, stir 2 min. Add garlic, stir until translucent, another 1–2 min.",
      "min": 4
    },
    {
      "t": "Pressure cook",
      "x": "Add basil, tomato paste, broth, tomatoes, chicken, salt, pepper and the dried tortellini. Stir gently to submerge. Seal lid, valve to sealing. Pressure cook 9 min high if using breast (11 min if leg/thigh). Quick release.",
      "min": 9
    },
    {
      "t": "Finish",
      "x": "Remove chicken, cube it, return to pot. Stir gently from here on; tortellini is delicate. Stir in spinach, Parmesan and warmed evaporated milk. Sauté briefly to wilt spinach and heat through. Serve.",
      "min": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Fresh spinach cut back to 1 cup since the tortellini filling already carries spinach flavour.",
    "Evaporated milk gives body without the split risk of fresh cream in a tomato soup."
  ]
